WEBVTT

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:06.040
In the name of the Father and of the Son and of the Holy Spirit, Amen.

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:13.120
The reading from the Sinoxadion from A23rd, on which we commemorate our righteous father,

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:18.320
Michael the Confessor, Bishop of Sinada.

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:24.080
On the 23rd of the month we celebrate the memory of our venerable father, Michael the Confessor,

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:27.520
Metropolitan of Sinada.

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:34.360
Born in Sinada, in Frigia, St. Michael early left his homeland for Constantinople, where

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:39.600
he linked himself in spiritual friendship with Saint Thelfiluctus.

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:44.840
The two young men showed such great unity of thought and feeling that they were seen

00:00:44.840 --> 00:00:47.760
as one new man.

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:53.880
When St. Tarasius, after having received the monastic habit was raised to patriarchal dignity,

00:00:53.880 --> 00:01:00.880
the two friends became monks in their turn in the monastery he had founded on the Bosphorus.

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:06.240
Rivaling each other in ascetic striving, they made rapid progress in virtue, enhanced by

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:12.440
the glorious adornment of humility and the constant gaiety of their souls.

00:01:12.440 --> 00:01:20.020
Tharasius informed of their great feats, appointed them Scevo-Filaxes of the Great Church, and

00:01:20.020 --> 00:01:27.860
shortly afterwards succeeded in making them against their will, except episcopal consecration.

00:01:27.860 --> 00:01:36.060
Thelfiluctus as Metropolitan of Nicomedia and Michael to be pastor of his homeland, Sinada.

00:01:36.060 --> 00:01:42.940
Rightly proclaiming the word of truth both by his teaching and his life, patient and merciful,

00:01:42.940 --> 00:01:49.380
having overcome anger, this good shepherd had churches and monasteries built and founded

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:56.900
hospices and charitable institutions to help the sick, the destitute and the strangers.

00:01:56.900 --> 00:02:04.220
Bishop Michael was present at the Second Council of Nicaea in 787, where he upheld the Orthodox

00:02:04.220 --> 00:02:12.220
doctrine of the veneration of the Holy icons, then on returning to his diocese quietly resumed

00:02:12.220 --> 00:02:14.860
his pastoral work.

00:02:14.860 --> 00:02:22.740
In 806, the year in which the Holy Patriarch Nicaferos succeeded the departed St. Tharasius,

00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:30.540
St. Michael was sent by Emperor Nicaferos to lead an embassy to Caliph Harun Al-Rashid,

00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:38.580
in the course of which he gave proof of all his qualities as a man of peace and conciliation.

00:02:38.580 --> 00:02:45.000
In the autumn of 811, he was sent to Rome as Patriarch Nicaferos' legate to present his

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:51.100
synodical letters to the Pope and to assure him of his support concerning the veneration

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:53.380
of the Holy icons.

00:02:53.380 --> 00:03:00.140
The following year he was received by Charlemagne at Ex-Lashapella and secured a peace treaty

00:03:00.140 --> 00:03:01.860
with him.

00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:09.580
After he had reigned for two years, the new emperor, Leo V, the Armenian, unveiled his

00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:16.020
dark designs and restarted the persecution against the Holy icons, St. Michael immediately

00:03:16.020 --> 00:03:22.660
allied himself with the defenders of the true faith, who had gathered with Patriarch Nicaferos,

00:03:22.660 --> 00:03:32.140
Othemias of Sardis, Joseph of Thessalonica, Emilianos of Zizekus, the Ophiloptus of Nicomedia,

00:03:32.140 --> 00:03:39.580
and many others, clergy, monks, and layfolk who held themselves ready to shed their blood

00:03:39.580 --> 00:03:41.540
for the faith.

00:03:41.540 --> 00:03:46.340
They presented themselves before the sovereign and tried to bring him to reason, both with

00:03:46.340 --> 00:03:51.380
arguments taken from the Holy Fathers and by reminding him of the support they had from

00:03:51.380 --> 00:04:00.100
the Church of Rome, but it was in vain, and, blinded by his fury, the tyrant had them arrested

00:04:00.100 --> 00:04:07.660
and sent into exile far from one another and with a ban on their corresponding.

00:04:07.660 --> 00:04:14.360
St. Michael was sent to Odysseus and Fridia, where he remained for more than ten years,

00:04:14.360 --> 00:04:20.900
suffering all the ill-treatment he received with thanksgiving and praying for his persecutors.

00:04:20.900 --> 00:04:25.740
He would not for anything cease defending the Orthodox faith and being ready to help

00:04:25.740 --> 00:04:34.920
the unfortunate, and he maintained unchanged his program of ascetic life and nocturnal prayer.

00:04:34.920 --> 00:04:40.620
He worked many miracles there, healing by his prayer and the honey of his words, both men

00:04:40.620 --> 00:04:47.620
and domestic animals, and succeeded in taming and converting the rough and uncouth inhabitants

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:50.620
of this remote region.

00:04:50.620 --> 00:04:56.580
The emperor, learning that exile was turning for the saint into an increase of glory, ordered

00:04:56.580 --> 00:04:59.500
that he be transferred somewhere else.

00:04:59.500 --> 00:05:05.220
Wandering hither and thither, the man of God came to a land infested with a multitude of rats

00:05:05.220 --> 00:05:07.900
that were ravaging the crops.

00:05:07.900 --> 00:05:13.740
He explained to his inhabitants that the plague had been sent by God as a punishment for their

00:05:13.740 --> 00:05:20.100
sins, and ordered them to spend three days in fasting and repentance.

00:05:20.100 --> 00:05:25.820
In this time had passed, he called them to go, all together into the fields.

00:05:25.820 --> 00:05:32.660
While the people cried, Kirie Eleison, the saint knelt and interceded for them, his hands

00:05:32.660 --> 00:05:35.900
and eyes turned heavenward.

00:05:35.900 --> 00:05:42.020
An earthquake immediately shook the region, and all the rats perished.

00:05:42.020 --> 00:05:47.580
Moving to another place called Oranticia, the inhabitants begged him to pray that they be

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:52.780
delivered from the uncountable hordes of grasshoppers, which were ruining their crops

00:05:52.780 --> 00:05:57.060
and fruit trees, threatening them with famine.

00:05:57.060 --> 00:06:02.580
The saint spent the night in prayer, and early in the morning went at the head of a procession,

00:06:02.580 --> 00:06:08.420
in which all the people of the land took part, singing Kirie Eleison.

00:06:08.420 --> 00:06:17.540
The grasshoppers gathered together on a thick, dark cloud which rose into the air and disappeared.

00:06:17.540 --> 00:06:23.180
The saint continued his wanderings, driven from place to place, shedding God's mercy on

00:06:23.180 --> 00:06:25.660
men and on their crops.

00:06:25.660 --> 00:06:32.500
Finally, after having spent some time in prison in Constantinople, he was exiled once more

00:06:32.500 --> 00:06:39.020
to the shore of the lake of Nicomedia, where other confessors of the faith were waiting until

00:06:39.020 --> 00:06:45.420
the good pleasure of Emperor Michael, the Stammerer, allowed them to rejoin their dioceses or

00:06:45.420 --> 00:06:48.140
monasteries.

00:06:48.140 --> 00:06:54.540
Aged more than 90, exhausted by his trials, Saint Michael continued no less to pray for the

00:06:54.540 --> 00:07:00.540
emperor, for the peace of the church, for the salvation of the world, and for the abundance

00:07:00.540 --> 00:07:03.540
of the fruits of the earth.

00:07:03.540 --> 00:07:09.620
On the Monday of Pentecost in the year 826, while leaving a meal organized by his longtime

00:07:09.620 --> 00:07:14.300
friend Saint Theodore, the stoodite, with whom he had never stopped corresponding during

00:07:14.300 --> 00:07:22.380
his exile, the holy prelate seized with a sudden malady, had to take to his bed.

00:07:22.380 --> 00:07:29.620
On the next day, Theodore found him in the throes of terrible pain, and on the third day,

00:07:29.620 --> 00:07:36.280
the Wednesday of Pentecost, Saint Michael, who had lost the power of speech, breathed his

00:07:36.360 --> 00:07:46.000
last, in the presence of his friend and companion, in striving, after forty years of episcopate.

00:07:46.000 --> 00:07:51.920
His lifeless body, Saint Theodore writes, looked like an angel, and shone with flashes of

00:07:51.920 --> 00:07:59.640
divine light, which so many years of prayer and contemplation had imprinted on it.

00:07:59.640 --> 00:08:04.920
The relic of his precious head, offered as a gift to the great Lavra of Saint Athanasios

00:08:04.920 --> 00:08:12.920
on Athos by Emperor Basil II and his brother Constantine VIII in 978, lies venerated there

00:08:12.920 --> 00:08:20.400
to the present day, and continues to work miracles to protect the crops from predatory animals,

00:08:20.400 --> 00:08:27.440
both those belonging to the monastery, and those in the regions to which it is sent.

00:08:27.440 --> 00:08:34.440
Under the prayers of our holy fathers, O Lord, Jesus Christ our God, have mercy on us,

00:08:34.440 --> 00:08:35.200
and save us.
